
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">&#8220;AI systems&#8230; will transform the discipline: they will make philosophy more capital-intensive. &#8220;</p>



<span id="more-27089"></span>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The following is a guest post by <a href="https://dstrohmaier.com/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">David Strohmaier</a>, a philosopher and computer scientist in the <a href="http://www.cl.cam.ac.uk/research/nl/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Natural Language and Information Processing</a> group at the University of Cambridge. In it, he explains why he thinks it&#8217;s reasonable to believe that AI systems will eventually have the capacities to &#8220;drive&#8221; philosophy, and how this will change the economics of philosophy.</p>



